a:2:{s:5:"items";a:4:{i:0;a:18:{s:6:"postid";s:3:"196";s:8:"parentid";s:1:"0";s:7:"forumid";s:1:"2";s:7:"topicid";s:3:"161";s:6:"userid";s:1:"1";s:5:"title";s:20:"New manager showdown";s:4:"body";s:499:"<p><a href="https://www42.myfantasyleague.com/2024/options?L=67102&amp;F=0004&amp;O=07" target="_blank" rel="noopener">We have an opening with the exit of sexy chocolate. I have received multiple requests to consider new managers. Now is the time to make your case in a reply here. Explain who the person is and why they are the best fit for this league, make sure it’s a good case because we are going to be voting on this Who really wants to take over this awful sexy chocolate roster? </a></p>";s:7:"created";s:19:"2024-07-22 17:04:08";s:8:"modified";s:19:"2024-07-22 17:05:57";s:5:"likes";s:1:"0";s:5:"votes";s:1:"0";s:9:"is_answer";s:1:"0";s:13:"is_first_post";s:1:"1";s:6:"status";s:1:"0";s:4:"name";s:0:"";s:5:"email";s:0:"";s:7:"private";s:1:"0";s:4:"root";s:1:"0";}i:1;a:18:{s:6:"postid";s:3:"197";s:8:"parentid";s:1:"0";s:7:"forumid";s:1:"2";s:7:"topicid";s:3:"161";s:6:"userid";s:2:"12";s:5:"title";s:24:"RE: New manager showdown";s:4:"body";s:644:"<p style="font-weight: 400">I’ve got to give a solid endorsement to Reginald Creech for the open fantasy football manager position. With over a decade of experience under his belt, Reginald mastered the art of managing salary caps, making savvy trades, drafting top-notch players and pushing for that competitive edge. Plus, Reginald brings a great sense of sportsmanship, always keeping things positive and fair while not being slack in trash talk. We’re looking for a manager with both expertise and a great attitude to bring into this awesome league, Reginal Creech is the perfect choice. - Hitman</p>
<p style="font-weight: 400"> </p>";s:7:"created";s:19:"2024-07-25 00:05:50";s:8:"modified";s:19:"2024-07-25 00:05:50";s:5:"likes";s:1:"0";s:5:"votes";s:1:"1";s:9:"is_answer";s:1:"0";s:13:"is_first_post";s:1:"0";s:6:"status";s:1:"0";s:4:"name";s:0:"";s:5:"email";s:0:"";s:7:"private";s:1:"0";s:4:"root";s:2:"-1";}i:2;a:18:{s:6:"postid";s:3:"201";s:8:"parentid";s:1:"0";s:7:"forumid";s:1:"2";s:7:"topicid";s:3:"161";s:6:"userid";s:5:"53536";s:5:"title";s:24:"RE: New manager showdown";s:4:"body";s:2966:"<p><strong>Profile: Eric “The Armament Guru” Harris</strong></p>
<p><strong>Bio:</strong> Meet Eric “The Armament Guru” Harris—a man whose life is as meticulously planned as his Fantasy Football draft strategy. A retired USAF Veteran with more medals than your average fantasy football owner has trophies, Eric has been the undisputed commander of our deployed 14-man Fantasy Football League for over a decade. His ability to keep the league alive through turnover crises is nothing short of legendary—like a fantasy football phoenix rising from the ashes of roster chaos.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> From sunny Florida, where the beaches are as hot as his draft picks. Yes, while others enjoy the sun, Eric is inside, meticulously studying player stats and scouting reports, all while balancing family life and FSU Seminole pride.</p>
<p><strong>Family Status:</strong> A proud “Girl-Dad” who’s probably used to dodging princess tiaras and negotiating bedtime deals like he’s strategizing a military operation. Married to his beautiful Wife, Lia, he’s mastered the art of compromise—whether it’s convincing his wife that his fantasy football research is a “team-building exercise” or explaining why he absolutely <em>needed</em> that extra draft pick.</p>
<p><strong>Fantasy Football Skills:</strong> Eric is the F-15SA Armament Specialist of Fantasy Football—precision, power, and perfect aim. His league management skills are so sharp they could slice through a defensive line. His strategy is so well-tuned that if Fantasy Football were a combat mission, he’d be the general everyone calls when they need a win.</p>
<p><strong>Fan Credentials:</strong> A die-hard FSU Seminoles fan, Eric is no stranger to the highs and lows of college football. His loyalty to the ‘Noles is matched only by his commitment to his fantasy team. Don’t be surprised if you see him in a garnet and gold jersey while he’s orchestrating his draft like a maestro conducting a symphony of stats and spreadsheets.  Eric also needs a Support Group for Fantasy…he’s been playing since 1999, and is currently the Commish for our down-range league, as well as an owner in a long-running league since 2008!</p>
<p><strong>Fun Fact:</strong> Eric once managed to keep a straight face when his entire league thought he was giving away his draft strategy in a “live” video—turns out he was just practicing his poker face for the next big trade.</p>
<p><strong>Summary:</strong> If you’re looking for a Fantasy Football owner who combines military precision with family-first values and a deep passion for football, look no further than Eric. He’s got the experience, the dedication, and the Seminole spirit to take your fantasy league to the next level—just make sure to avoid any “friendly” trades unless you’re prepared for a battle of epic proportions!</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p>-Peace,</p>
